< Yellowfin images from Majuro were uploaded to the online computer vision platform Roboflow \citep{roboflow2020} for what is referred to as `ground-truth' annotation. Coral experts in the Cohen Laboratory at WHOI outlined individual colonies with polygonal masks, using Roboflow's Smart Select tool, which leverages the Segment Anything Model~2 (SAM2) \citep{ravi2024sam2} to generate first-pass masks, which were then manually fine tuned to accurately outline the colonies. Each image's annotations were reviewed by a senior lab member to ensure accuracy, although inter-annotator agreement statistics were not collected. Annotators labeled corals to the highest degree of taxonomic resolution, and up to 82 distinct labels were identified, reflective of the high biodiversity of the Majuro reef system. Over the course of two months, WHOI's annotation team hand-annotated 552 images for a total of 14,275 individual masks.
