< The first stage of the proposed machine vision pipeline involves instance segmentation with SAM2, a foundation model developed by Meta AI for promptable image segmentation based on a Vision Transformer (ViT) encoder-decoder architecture. Given the heterogeneity of coral structures across size scales and the variance across Yellowfin images, we adopt a two-stream configuration of SAM2, tuned conjointly to capture both large and small coral colonies. A single, jointly-tuned SAM2 configuration, was initially explored, but found it could not simultaneously serve both size regimes well: hyperparameters tuned to reliably fragment and recover many small colonies (e.g.\ a dense prompt grid, permissive stability thresholds) over-propose small, spurious masks in scenes dominated by one or two large colonies, while hyperparameters tuned for conservative, high-precision large-colony masks miss small or fragmented colonies entirely. Since a single image can contain either regime (or both), no single configuration's optimum served both well, motivating two separately-tuned configurations reconciled downstream by mask consolidation. Each image is passed through both configurations in parallel, generating potentially overlapping sets of candidate mask proposals that are later reconciled through a mask consolidation algorithm.
---
