< Second, while model predictions generally performed well, the observed underestimations of average coral cover and bleaching rates are ecologically meaningful and should be considered when interpreting the results. Managers looking to incorporate the predictions of any machine learning model should be aware of the specific biases of that model and training iteration. Future work involving training iterations of the model presented here with new training data should examine whether these biases persist across different reef domains and image capture methods.
