> First, the generalizability of our results is constrained by the data domain. All images were collected by the Yellowfin Surfzone ASV over a large patch reef in the northwest of Majuro, Marshall Islands. This narrow capture space may induce distributional shift when applied to sites with different environmental conditions even across sites in Majuro. We do not view this as a defect of the proposed pipeline so much as a starting point: the modular design (Figure~\ref{fig:pipeline}) is intended to support continued retraining as annotated imagery from additional reef systems becomes available, with the SAM2 tuning, CNN submodels, and ensemble combiner each independently updatable without redesigning the pipeline. Demonstrating this multi-site extension empirically is future work, contingent on acquiring comparably annotated surveys from other reef systems.
