< Seventh, our estimates of coral cover are computed as a Euclidean projection on the image plane, ignoring vertical relief. This limitation mirrors those of planar photographic surveys \citep{peerj954}, where estimates are biased relative to true three-dimensional rugosity. This is especially problematic for reefs with steep inclines or vertical walls, where the area of available reef substrate is much greater than the 2D planar area. 
